THIRD-PARTY DERIVATIONS

This project includes an "Autopilot Provider" adapter
(src/autopilot-provider.ts) whose method structure and command
translation semantics are derived from:

    pypilot-autopilot-provider
    Copyright (c) Panaaj
    https://github.com/panaaj/pypilot-autopilot-provider
    Apache License 2.0

The upstream project ships its own socket.io client. In our fork we
re-implemented the same command surface on top of the PypilotClient we
already carry (src/pypilot-client.ts) so that a Signal K server with
both plugins effectively active only ever opens ONE socket to the
pypilot_web process on the TinyPilot. This is a functional benefit for
Pi Zero W hardware; no derivative works of the upstream code itself
are distributed.

Apache-2.0 code is compatible with AGPL-3.0 for inclusion — the Apache
portions retain their original license notice inside our source; the
combined work is distributed under AGPL-3.0-or-later.


PYPILOT UPSTREAM (INTERPROCESS ONLY, NOT LINKED)

For the socket.io protocol layer talking to pypilot_web
(watch=, name=value) we independently confirmed it against the
upstream pypilot sources (https://github.com/pypilot/pypilot) which
are LGPL-3.0. We do NOT link the pypilot code into this plugin. The
plugin communicates with a separate pypilot_web process over a TCP
socket, which does not trigger LGPL's linking requirements.
